<h2 id="what-the-storage-layout-offers">What the storage layout offers</h2>
<p>Capacity is split into <strong>308 litres for fresh food and 128 litres for frozen food</strong>. The bottom mount arrangement keeps the fridge above the freezer, which may suit a household that reaches for fresh ingredients more often than frozen meals.</p>

<p>LG lists three fridge shelves, four door baskets, a vegetable drawer and three transparent freezer drawers. Before buying, think about the awkward items in your own shop: a large food container, tall drink bottles, a whole cauliflower or a wide frozen pizza. A litre figure cannot tell you whether those will fit conveniently.</p>

<p>The <a href="https://www.lg.com/au/fridge-freezers/bottom-mount/gb-b400ps/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Australian specifications</a> list no folding shelf, wine rack or Fresh Converter drawer for this range, even though some shared gallery illustrations show extra storage features. Check the exact display unit rather than assuming every pictured accessory is included.</p>

<p>There is a normal ice tray, but no automatic ice maker or water dispenser. That leaves the buying decision centred on food storage and kitchen fit. If chilled water or automatic ice is a priority, compare a model designed to provide it.</p>

<h2 id="energy-use-and-connected-features">Energy use and connected features</h2>
<p>LG publishes <strong>5.5 stars and 261 kWh per year</strong> for these models. At an illustrative electricity usage rate of 30 cents per kWh, that works out to about <strong>$78 a year</strong>; at 40 cents, about <strong>$104</strong>. These are calculations from the rated consumption, not measurements from our use. Room temperature, settings and door opening affect actual consumption.</p>

<p>ThinQ Wi-Fi connectivity allows compatible phones to adjust settings and access diagnostic functions. Express Cool, Express Freeze and a door alarm are also listed. The app requires a compatible phone, Wi-Fi and registration; it is worth considering whether you would use those functions beyond the initial setup.</p>

<p>LG currently lists security updates until <strong>31 December 2031</strong>. That support date matters if connectivity is part of the attraction, and is separate from the physical lifespan of the appliance.</p>

<h2 id="warranty-and-the-delivery-quote">Warranty and the delivery quote</h2>
<p>LG’s <a href="https://www.lg.com/au/support/warranty/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Australian warranty information</a> provides two years of product parts and labour cover. The advertised ten-year compressor cover is parts-only after the initial product warranty: the published structure adds three years of sealed-system parts cover, then five further years for the compressor part. It does not promise ten years of labour-free repairs. Australian Consumer Law rights also apply.</p>

<p>Before paying, get a total delivered price that includes the services you need: positioning, packaging removal, taking away the old fridge and any door reversal. Confirm whether a delivery crew will negotiate stairs or tight turns, rather than assuming a standard delivery includes them.</p>

<h2 id="who-this-range-is-worth-a-look-for">Who this range is worth a look for</h2>
<p>The Fit &amp; Max range is worth inspecting if you want a bottom mount fridge, a choice of finishes and less wasted space at the sides. The hinge design is especially relevant where the fridge sits beside a wall or tall cupboard, provided the full installation and opening measurements work.</p>

<p>It will be less suitable if you need a much larger freezer, automatic ice or a water dispenser. Long-term owner evidence is still limited: the exact Matte White listing we checked on ProductReview.com.au had no owner reviews, and The Good Guys showed no reviews for these listings. Our first look supports a closer inspection of the fit and features, rather than a reliability verdict.</p>

<p>For a larger French door alternative, see our <a href="/guides/fisher-paykel-precision-fit-fridge-preview/">Fisher &amp; Paykel Precision Fit preview</a>. Its capacity, water features and installation requirements are different, so compare the actual opening and storage layout before comparing the styling.</p>

